# tests/litscan/handoff.rxt -- [K82] (B), THE HANDOFF: the run pre-check's first
# window hit c, less K, becomes the search body's scan start
# (docs/design/litscan_k82h.md §4.2 item 2; docs/spec/tuning.md §2.41).
#
# Written by gen_handoff.py; every expectation is an oracle's: a `byte` block's
# from python3 `re` AND libpcre2 (which must agree), a `utf8` block's from
# libpcre2 under PCRE2_UTF | PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF alone (so `# pcre2-only`:
# the harness's python tier reads subjects as latin-1), as is a byte block
# python cannot compile (\G, \K). Cells sit at EVERY
# character-boundary start position, because the handoff moves where a scan
# begins. Each block is written on the default route and under `engine vm`,
# the forced VM with no DFA scan: the same cells (its attempt loop hands off
# too, [REQRUN-VM], handoff_vm.rxt). The rows are the design's witnesses: the maximum offset on
# all three routes (the unanchored scan's reverse pass is bounded by
# search_from, so a K one byte short only shows on the attempt and hybrid
# routes), two occurrences (the gate's leftmost contract), a decoy, multibyte
# width, ill-formed text before the window, seeded starts, \G on the attempt
# route and on the hybrid (whose prefilter reads its third argument as \G),
# \K, find-all subjects (dense and overlapping) and two unbounded controls;
# and [REQ-HANDOFF-L1]'s BYTE landmarks (ipv6-, ipv4- and dotted4-shaped,
# seeded, utf8, ill-formed) whose forward scan RE-ENTERS the handoff at each
# restart, the K admission's admitted and declined witnesses, and Frank's
# hostile cell a.{1,50000}z over z-dense text.

# K = 5, unanchored DFA: the match begins K bytes before the window; startpos 1..5 cross the clamp (S470)
pattern x{2,5}(?i:cat)
features all
encoding byte
ms 0 "xxxxxCaT" 0 8
ms 1 "xxxxxCaT" 1 8
ms 2 "xxxxxCaT" 2 8
ms 3 "xxxxxCaT" 3 8
ns 4 "xxxxxCaT"
ns 5 "xxxxxCaT"
ns 6 "xxxxxCaT"
ns 7 "xxxxxCaT"
ns 8 "xxxxxCaT"
ms 0 "xxxxxcat" 0 8
ms 1 "xxxxxcat" 1 8
ms 2 "xxxxxcat" 2 8
ms 3 "xxxxxcat" 3 8
ns 4 "xxxxxcat"
ns 5 "xxxxxcat"
ns 6 "xxxxxcat"
ns 7 "xxxxxcat"
ns 8 "xxxxxcat"
ms 0 "zxxxxxcat" 1 9
ms 1 "zxxxxxcat" 1 9
ms 2 "zxxxxxcat" 2 9
ms 3 "zxxxxxcat" 3 9
ms 4 "zxxxxxcat" 4 9
ns 5 "zxxxxxcat"
ns 6 "zxxxxxcat"
ns 7 "zxxxxxcat"
ns 8 "zxxxxxcat"
ns 9 "zxxxxxcat"
ms 0 "xxcat" 0 5
ns 1 "xxcat"
ns 2 "xxcat"
ns 3 "xxcat"
ns 4 "xxcat"
ns 5 "xxcat"
ms 0 "xxxxxxcat" 1 9
ms 1 "xxxxxxcat" 1 9
ms 2 "xxxxxxcat" 2 9
ms 3 "xxxxxxcat" 3 9
ms 4 "xxxxxxcat" 4 9
ns 5 "xxxxxxcat"
ns 6 "xxxxxxcat"
ns 7 "xxxxxxcat"
ns 8 "xxxxxxcat"
ns 9 "xxxxxxcat"
ms 0 "\x0axxxxxcat" 1 9
ms 1 "\x0axxxxxcat" 1 9
ms 2 "\x0axxxxxcat" 2 9
ms 3 "\x0axxxxxcat" 3 9
ms 4 "\x0axxxxxcat" 4 9
ns 5 "\x0axxxxxcat"
ns 6 "\x0axxxxxcat"
ns 7 "\x0axxxxxcat"
ns 8 "\x0axxxxxcat"
ns 9 "\x0axxxxxcat"

